# Boeffla generic wakelock blocker (andip71, v1.1.0) - in-tree
# integration for odin 5.4. The source copy is taken from the
# blu_spark lineage (engstk/op7), which already ships an empty
# compiled-in default list; see SOURCE.md in this directory.
# Default stays n on purpose: scripts/build-kernel.sh enables this
# symbol explicitly for the resukisu variant only, so every other
# variant/config path stays bit-identical to the verified builds.

config BOEFFLA_WL_BLOCKER
	bool "Boeffla generic wakelock blocker driver"
	depends on PM
	default n
	help
	  Block selected kernel wakelocks by name on the wakeup_source
	  activation path (drivers/base/power/wakeup.c). The block lists
	  are runtime sysfs knobs under
	  /sys/class/misc/boeffla_wakelock_blocker/ (wakelock_blocker
	  and wakelock_blocker_default, semicolon-separated names).

	  The compiled-in default list is EMPTY for odin: with no names
	  configured, wl_blocker_active stays false, the wakeup.c hook
	  is a no-op and suspend behaviour is identical to a kernel
	  without this driver. Only add names at runtime, after checking
	  /sys/kernel/wakeup_sources on the real device.
